# Version

## Current Version

`0.8.0`

## Version Type

Minor workflow-feature release over `0.7.7`.

This version implements Phase 4B deterministic document ingestion, OCR fallback, and multi-candidate recruitment examples in `@office-dsl/example-runner`. The runner discovers `examples-recruitment` scenarios, loads `oferta.md`, `cv.md`, and `cv.pdf`, extracts deterministic text-PDF fixtures, routes scanned/image-only fixture PDFs through mock OCR text, normalizes sourced offer/CV content into partial Intent/Contract DSL, generates per-candidate proposals, reuses the Human1/Human2 chat runner for negotiation, and writes `out/contract.dsl.txt` only for candidates whose chat reaches bilateral approval of the same current contract hash.

The Phase 4B implementation is deterministic and mock-safe. It validates the folder convention and fixture workflow end to end, but it does not install or call a production OCR provider, external PDF service, or live recruitment backend. CLI/backend/UI surfacing for canonical approvals and production document-ingestion surfaces remains open in later phases.

